+# CATCH under APPS on the board (arcade's unit 078, soroban's gate; stu32-arcade docs/catch.md): GAMES's second
+# page (K5, more) lists SALVO, 3720, MOLES and CATCH, so CATCH is K3 there. ENTER plays gentle. Catches depend on the
+# seed, so the walls tell a live key from a dead one: from the middle, 4 held reaches the left wall in 1.5 s and
+# bumps once (100 Hz, 10 ms); 6 held crosses to the right wall in about 3 s and bumps; SOFT1 and SOFT6 the same; +
+# held moves nothing and bumps nothing. The rules are the host's check (make catchcheck). C ends CATCH, and
+# 2 ENTER 3 + must give 5.
+send RESTART
+wait STANDIN READY 30
+# C twice first, then X = 4, so the closing 2 ENTER 3 + = 5 can fail (soroban's shape, 6388bc4)
+send K42
+send U42
+send K42
+send U42
+send K38
+send U38
+send K18
+send U18
+send K38
+send U38
+send K46
+send U46
+send X
+expect X=4
+send X
+expect stack-free
+send K36
+send U36
+send K43
+send U43
+sleep 1
+send K1
+send U1
+sleep 1
+send K5
+send U5
+sleep 1
+send K3
+send U3
+sleep 1
+send X
+expect app: CATCH
+send K18
+send U18
+sleep 1
+send K31
+expect tone: app 100 Hz 10 ms 3
+send U31
+send K33
+expect tone: app 100 Hz 10 ms 5
+send U33
+send K0
+expect tone: app 100 Hz 10 ms 5
+send U0
+send K5
+expect tone: app 100 Hz 10 ms 5
+send U5
+send K46
+expect-none tone: app 100 Hz 4
+send U46
+send X
+expect-min stack-free 2048
+expect app: CATCH
+send K42
+send U42
+sleep 1
+send X
+expect app: -
+send K38
+send U38
+send K18
+send U18
+send K39
+send U39
+send K46
+send U46
+send X
+expect X=5
